$academyConfig['rich_lessons']['*']['spaceflight-robotics']=[
 space_lesson('Why Rockets Work','Rocket propulsion','A rocket accelerates exhaust backward and gains forward momentum. It works in vacuum because thrust does not require pushing against air.','Relate exhaust speed and propellant flow to thrust.','Rocket motion follows conservation of momentum and Newton’s third law.','A balloon moves when air escapes in the opposite direction.','rocket'),
 space_lesson('Forces During Launch','Newton’s laws','Thrust must overcome weight and drag, while acceleration changes as propellant is consumed. Structural loads and vibration shape the vehicle.','Draw a force diagram for liftoff and ascent.','Mission engineering begins by identifying forces, constraints, and changing mass.','A rocket begins rising when upward thrust exceeds downward weight and drag.','forces'),
 space_lesson('Staging and the Rocket Equation','Mass efficiency','Discarding empty tanks and engines reduces mass. The rocket equation shows why carrying propellant to carry more propellant becomes difficult.','Compare a single-stage and staged mission concept.','Small mass savings can create large mission benefits.','Multi-stage launch vehicles drop hardware that is no longer useful.','rocket'),
 space_lesson('Reaching and Changing Orbit','Orbital manoeuvres','A launch gives sideways velocity; burns change the orbit’s energy and shape. Transfer orbits trade time, fuel, and geometry.','Plan a simplified transfer from low Earth orbit to a higher orbit.','Burn direction matters: thrust along motion raises orbital energy, while opposite thrust lowers it.','A Hohmann transfer uses two carefully timed burns between circular orbits.','orbit'),
 space_lesson('Navigation and Communication','Deep-space operations','Missions use radio tracking, star sensors, inertial systems, clocks, and orbital models. Signal delay grows with distance.','Create a communication plan for Mars including delay and safe modes.','A distant spacecraft must handle many problems autonomously because commands are not instant.','A one-way Earth–Mars radio signal can take several to more than twenty minutes.','navigation'),
 space_lesson('Keeping Humans Alive','Life-support systems','Crewed missions must manage oxygen, carbon dioxide, water, food, temperature, pressure, waste, fire, and radiation.','Design a closed-loop water and air flow diagram.','Life support is a connected system; one failure can affect many others.','The International Space Station recycles much of its water.','life-support'),
 space_lesson('Satellites in Everyday Life','Satellite systems','Satellites support weather forecasting, navigation, communication, science, environmental monitoring, and disaster response.','Match a public need to orbit, sensor, power, and ground system.','A satellite is only one part of a service that also requires launch, control, data processing, and users.','Weather satellites combine multiple wavelengths to track clouds, moisture, temperature, and fires.','satellite'),
 space_lesson('Robots Before Humans','Robotic exploration','Flybys, orbiters, landers, rovers, aircraft, and sample-return missions offer different coverage, risk, and complexity.','Select a robotic architecture for a hazardous destination.','Mission form should follow the science question and environment.','A rover provides detailed local geology while an orbiter maps broad regions.','robot'),
 space_lesson('Human Factors and Ethics','Responsible exploration','Isolation, workload, communication, health, teamwork, debris, contamination, and international responsibilities affect mission design.','Write a crew and planetary-protection risk register.','Exploration is a human system as well as a technical system.','A strong mission plan includes psychological safety and responsible treatment of other worlds.','mission'),
 space_lesson('Capstone: Design a Space Mission','Systems engineering','Define the mission question, success criteria, spacecraft, instruments, trajectory, operations, risks, and public value.','Present a mission review with evidence and defend one engineering tradeoff.','A complete mission connects science, engineering, people, budget, time, and risk.','A smaller instrument suite may improve reliability and still answer the highest-priority question.','mission'),
