$academyConfig['rich_lessons']['*']['astrobiology-exoplanets']=[
 space_lesson('What Does Life Need?','Habitability','Known life needs chemistry, energy, and an environment that allows complex reactions. Liquid water is useful but not a guarantee of life.','Separate requirements, helpful conditions, and assumptions.','Habitability describes possibility; inhabited requires evidence.','A dark ocean beneath ice could use chemical energy instead of sunlight.','habitability'),
 space_lesson('The Habitable Zone','Orbital climate','The circumstellar habitable zone is where surface liquid water might persist under suitable atmospheric conditions.','Compare two planets around different stars.','Distance from a star matters, but atmosphere, geology, rotation, and history also shape climate.','Venus and Mars show why location alone does not determine habitability.','habitable-zone'),
 space_lesson('Mars: Past and Present','Mars exploration','Valleys, minerals, sediments, ice, and rover observations show that ancient Mars had liquid water environments.','Build an evidence table for ancient habitability.','Evidence of a habitable environment is not evidence that life existed there.','Perseverance is caching samples selected for future laboratory study.','mars'),
 space_lesson('Ocean Worlds','Europa and Enceladus','Tidal heating may maintain salty oceans beneath ice. Plumes and surface chemistry offer possible ways to sample them.','Compare a plume fly-through with an ice-penetrating lander.','An ocean, chemistry, and energy make ocean moons high-priority astrobiology targets.','Cassini detected water-rich plumes erupting from Enceladus.','moon-mission'),
 space_lesson('Finding Exoplanets','Detection methods','Transits reveal periodic dimming; radial velocity detects stellar motion; imaging, microlensing, and timing reach other systems.','Identify which signal belongs to each method.','Most methods reveal a planet indirectly, so repeated signals and independent checks matter.','A transit can estimate planet size relative to its star.','exoplanet'),
 space_lesson('Reading Alien Atmospheres','Atmospheric spectra','During a transit, some starlight filters through an atmosphere. Spectra can suggest gases, clouds, temperature, and chemistry.','Interpret a simplified transmission spectrum.','One molecule rarely proves life; context and combinations of gases matter.','Water vapour can be scientifically exciting without being a biosignature by itself.','spectrum'),
 space_lesson('Extremophiles on Earth','Life at limits','Earth organisms live in acidic, salty, cold, hot, dry, pressurized, and radiation-rich environments. They expand—but do not remove—the limits we consider.','Connect an extremophile to an extraterrestrial analogue.','Earth is our only confirmed example of life, so conclusions must keep that limitation visible.','Microbes near hydrothermal vents use chemical energy without sunlight.','habitability'),
 space_lesson('Listening and Looking for Technology','Technosignatures','Searches examine unusual radio or optical signals, atmospheric pollution, waste heat, and other possible technology signatures.','Design criteria that separate a candidate signal from interference.','Extraordinary claims require repeatable observations and careful elimination of ordinary explanations.','A signal that does not repeat cannot yet support a strong conclusion.','signal'),
 space_lesson('Planetary Protection','Responsible astrobiology','Forward contamination could harm another environment or confuse life-detection results; backward contamination requires safe sample handling.','Create a cleanliness and containment plan.','Protecting scientific integrity and environments is part of exploration.','Spacecraft for sensitive destinations undergo strict biological cleanliness controls.','protection'),
 space_lesson('Capstone: Evidence for Life Brief','Scientific argument','A strong claim connects observations to reasoning, alternatives, uncertainty, and the next test needed.','Write a mission briefing that ranks three possible biosignatures without overstating them.','Science advances through testable claims and transparent uncertainty, not certainty theatre.','A gas combination may be intriguing while geology remains a plausible alternative.','evidence'),
